                            <comment id="20372499" author="JIRAUSER129848" created="Wed, 29 Jul 2026 22:24:41 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/attachment/7107267/7107267_Demo+JGVT-3779.mov&quot; title=&quot;Demo JGVT-3779.mov attached to JGVT-3779&quot;&gt;Demo JGVT-3779.mov&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="20339621" author="JIRAUSER211903" created="Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:08:05 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=CSims11&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;CSims11&quot;&gt;Sims, Cody [JRDUS]&lt;/a&gt; I believe yes is the answer. As we never know when this one is will be used. We are only interested in individual admin actions made by a person. So yes you can also filter out the second service account.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="20315353" author="JIRAUSER129848" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:24:43 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=TVanDe17&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;TVanDe17&quot;&gt;Van den broeck, Tamara [JRDBE NON-J&amp;amp;J]&lt;/a&gt; The service account we&apos;ve been using is &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:sa-prd-signals@its.jnj.com&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;sa-prd-signals@its.jnj.com&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/images/icons/mail_small.gif&quot; height=&quot;12&quot; width=&quot;13&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; but there is also &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:sa-prd-gxpsignals@its.jnj.com&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;sa-prd-gxpsignals@its.jnj.com&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/images/icons/mail_small.gif&quot; height=&quot;12&quot; width=&quot;13&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .. should this second one also be filtered out by the &quot;User name in audit log is different from service account&quot; criteria?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="19991087" author="gklesse" created="Mon, 22 Jun 2026 16:19:14 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&#129302; &lt;b&gt;Automated Complexity Analysis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Estimate:&lt;/b&gt; M&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Files Affected:&lt;/b&gt; 3&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reasoning:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
This story requires investigating and potentially modifying the system audit trail API to include additional filtering capabilities for user role tracking. The work involves checking if new/old value data is available in the API and updating the audit trail to include an additional filter. This is a backend-only change that requires understanding existing audit trail patterns and adding moderate filtering logic.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Implementation Details:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Need to investigate the audit trail API to verify if new value/old value fields are available for user role changes. Update the audit trail query/filtering logic to support filtering by user creation method (automated vs manual administrator creation). Modify the audit trail data model or serializer to expose the additional filter parameter. Update the audit trail endpoint to accept and process the new filter criteria for identifying manually created users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Open Questions:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;What specific field in the audit trail distinguishes between automated vs manual user creation?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Is the new/old value data already captured in the audit trail or does it need to be added?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;What is the exact filter criteria needed - by user role, creation method, or both?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Does SDLC-0000097786 provide specific requirements for the filter implementation?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Risks:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Audit trail data may not currently capture sufficient information to distinguish manual vs automated user creation&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Changes to audit trail filtering could impact performance if not properly indexed&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;May need to coordinate with &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2569&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: download System Audit Trail report via web user interface&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-2569&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-2569&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to understand existing implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8212;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;This is an AI-generated complexity assessment based on the story description and codebase analysis. The development team has final authority on sizing decisions and may adjust this estimate based on their technical expertise and implementation approach. This assessment is meant to provide guidance, not to constrain technical decisions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
